// Delver of Secrets // Insectile Aberration — the first canon TRANSFORMING
// double-faced card ([CR#712.2]). The front's upkeep trigger reads the top card
// of your library (a full-info read, so the "look" is implicit in the
// condition) and MAY reveal an instant/sorcery to transform to the back
// ([CR#701.27a]). Mirrors the blessed Idris model (Cards.idr `card_DelverOfSecrets`):
// `If(Matches(Single(TopOfLibrary 1), Or([Instant, Sorcery])),
//     May(Sequentially([Reveal(Single(TopOfLibrary 1)), Transform(This)])))` —
// the top card is named DIRECTLY (`Single(TopOfLibrary(count: 1))`), no binder;
// "revealed this way" is English surface, not a distinct condition. First
// `Card::TwoFaced { layout: Transforming }` real card ([CR#712.8]: each face is
// a full set of characteristics).
TwoFaced(
    layout: Transforming,
    front: (
        name: "Delver of Secrets",
        mana_cost: [Blue],
        types: [Creature],
        subtypes: [Human, Wizard],
        abilities: [
            Triggered(
                event: StepBegins(at: Beginning(Upkeep), whose: Your),
                effect: If(
                    condition: Matches(
                        Single(TopOfLibrary(count: 1)),
                        Or([Type("Instant"), Type("Sorcery")]),
                    ),
                    then: May(effect: Sequentially([
                        Reveal(what: Single(TopOfLibrary(count: 1))),
                        Transform(This),
                    ])),
                ),
            ),
        ],
        power: 1,
        toughness: 1,
    ),
    back: (
        name: "Insectile Aberration",
        types: [Creature],
        subtypes: [Human, Insect],
        abilities: [Keyword(Flying)],
        power: 3,
        toughness: 2,
    ),
)
